  "version": "0.3.6",
  "notes": "**A clearer status line, and no false R2 warning on simplex.**\n\n- **The status line at the bottom shows only the latest event.** Several events side by side read like one sentence, and long ones ran off the edge. A long event now ends in \"\u2026\": hover over it for the full text. The full history is still in Diagnostics.\n- **No \"R2 is a gateway\" warning on simplex.** Icom radios keep R1 and R2 while duplex is off, but neither show nor send them. The IC-9700 still reports them over CI-V, so Aether DV warned about a gateway the radio wasn't using. The warning now appears only when Aether DV can't tell whether duplex is on. The test summary says \"simplex, R1/R2 stored, not sent on simplex\", \"duplex on\" or \"duplex unknown\".\n- **Sending resumes within seconds once the radio is put right.** When the radio's settings hold sending (for example DUP\u2212 on a simplex port), Aether DV now checks them every 10 seconds instead of every minute.\n\nStill **tested on the bench only**: two radios on simplex, no repeaters or D-RATS stations yet.",
